description: "mcp-skill-deployer: when the user explicitly asks to audit, score, optimize, inspect, or publish an MCP/Skill project, run compliance checks, quality scoring, guided optimization, and generate export files. Requires per-step user confirmation before any publish, push, or registry operation."
globs: "**/package.json,**/skills/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

When user explicitly asks to audit, optimize, inspect, package, or publish their MCP/Skill project:

1. Pick mode from intent: Audit (report only) / Optimize (confirmed edits) / Publish (full pipeline) — never default to publishing
2. Run read-only pre-flight audit (git status, secret scan, package.json / SKILL.md validation)
3. Score the project against the 100-point quality checklist (MCP or Skill) and output a graded report with prioritized fixes
4. Optimize: show diff preview per fix, apply only after per-item user confirmation, then re-score
5. Generate export files (never overwrite without asking)
6. Run tests and dry-run security checks
7. Ask user for confirmation before any npm publish / git push / registry submit
8. Print summary only — do not execute publish/push without user approval
